Input: {"question": "Which country does the Supreme Electoral Tribunal belong to?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d00", "start": 0, "end": 301, "text": "Superior Electoral Court The Superior Electoral Court (, TSE) is the highest body of the Brazilian Electoral Justice, which also comprises one Regional Electoral Court (, TRE) in each of the 26 states and the Federal District of the country, as determined by Article 118 of the Constitution of Brazil."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d00", "start": 302, "end": 482, "text": "The Brazilian Electoral Code of 1932 established the Electoral Justice in Brazil, replacing the political system conducted by the Legislative branch over the electoral proceedings."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d00", "start": 483, "end": 566, "text": "The new judicial system transferred control over such proceedings to the Judiciary."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d00", "start": 567, "end": 643, "text": "In the present, duties of the Electoral Justice are regulated by a posterior"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d01", "start": 0, "end": 89, "text": "the political system conducted by the Legislative branch over the electoral proceedings ."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d01", "start": 90, "end": 180, "text": "[ 2 ] The new judicial system transferred control over such proceedings to the Judiciary ."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d01", "start": 181, "end": 303, "text": "In the present , duties of the Electoral Justice are regulated by a posterior Electoral Code , approved in 1965 ( Law No ."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d01", "start": 304, "end": 415, "text": "4.737/65 ) , [ 3 ] which revoked the 1932 code , but kept the judicial control over the electoral proceedings ."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d01", "start": 416, "end": 558, "text": "The Superior Electoral Court is the highest judicial body of the Brazilian Electoral Justice as per the §3 of the Article 121 of the Brazilian"}, "D3S1": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d02", "start": 0, "end": 21, "text": "recounted by machine."}, "D3S2": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d02", "start": 22, "end": 149, "text": "[25] In the elections on 18 May 2003, there was an electronic voting problem reported where one candidate got 4096 extra votes."}, "D3S3": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d02", "start": 150, "end": 278, "text": "The error was only detected because she had more preferential votes than her own list, which is impossible in the voting system."}, "D3S4": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d02", "start": 279, "end": 413, "text": "The official explanation was the spontaneous inversion of a bit at the position 13 in the memory of the computer (i.e., a soft error)."}, "D3S5": {"document_number": 3, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d02", "start": 414, "end": 530, "text": "[26] Argentina edit Main article: Electronic voting in Argentina Electronic voting in Argentina was introduced in..."}, "D4S1": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03", "start": 0, "end": 33, "text": "Court of Bosnia and Herzegovina 9"}, "D4S2": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03", "start": 36, "end": 67, "text": "Court of Bosnia and Herzegovina"}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03", "start": 70, "end": 94, "text": "Botswana Court of Appeal"}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03", "start": 97, "end": 125, "text": "Brazil Supreme Federal Court"}, "D4S5": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03", "start": 128, "end": 184, "text": "Presidential nomination with Senate confirmation - 75 11"}, "D4S6": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03", "start": 187, "end": 215, "text": "Superior Court of Justice 33"}, "D4S7": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03", "start": 218, "end": 248, "text": "Brunei Supreme Court of Brunei"}, "D4S8": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03", "start": 251, "end": 302, "text": "Judicial Committee of the Privy Council (see below)"}, "D4S9": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03", "start": 305, "end": 352, "text": "Bulgaria Supreme Court of Cassation of Bulgaria"}, "D4S10": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03", "start": 355, "end": 395, "text": "Supreme Administrative Court of Bulgaria"}, "D4S11": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03", "start": 398, "end": 440, "text": "Burkina Faso Supreme Court of Burkina Faso"}, "D4S12": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03", "start": 443, "end": 475, "text": "Burundi Supreme Court of Burundi"}, "D4S13": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03", "start": 478, "end": 523, "text": "Cambodia Constitutional Council of Cambodia 9"}, "D4S14": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03", "start": 526, "end": 553, "text": "Supreme Court of Cambodia 9"}, "D4S15": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03", "start": 556, "end": 594, "text": "Cameroon Supreme Court of Cameroon [a]"}, "D4S16": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03", "start": 597, "end": 627, "text": "Canada Supreme Court of Canada"}, "D4S17": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03", "start": 630, "end": 664, "text": "Judicial appointments in Canada 75"}, "D4S18": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03", "start": 667, "end": 700, "text": "Canada Supreme Electoral Tribunal"}, "D4S19": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03", "start": 703, "end": 802, "text": "The Supreme Electoral Tribunal in Canada oversees the electoral process and ensures fair elections."}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d04", "start": 0, "end": 227, "text": "Supreme Electoral Tribunal (Honduras) The Supreme Electoral Tribunal (\"Tribunal Supremo Electoral\" in Spanish) is the highest electoral authority, both at the administrative and jurisdictional level in the Republic of Honduras."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d04", "start": 228, "end": 334, "text": "The Supreme Electoral Tribunal of Honduras deals with everything related to electoral acts and procedures."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d04", "start": 335, "end": 482, "text": "Integration, organization and operation are governed by the precepts of the Constitution of Honduras and the Electoral and Political Organizations."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d04", "start": 483, "end": 683, "text": "Insufficient requires of a budget of 700,0000 Lempiras, but only were assigned to it 400 millions, but part of this budget has to pay the debt of 125 millions purchased during the general elections of"}, "D6S1": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d05", "start": 0, "end": 10, "text": "Congress ."}, "D6S2": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d05", "start": 11, "end": 191, "text": "An independent entity , functionally unattached to all three branches of Government , the Public Ministry was instituted on January the 6th , 1994 , through Legislative Decree No ."}, "D6S3": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d05", "start": 192, "end": 200, "text": "228-93 ."}, "D6S4": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d05", "start": 201, "end": 427, "text": "Its main functions are the prosecution of all crimes and felonies , to ensure full compliance by all with the Constitution and the law of the land , and to represent , to defend and to protect the general interest of society ."}, "D6S5": {"document_number": 6, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d05", "start": 428, "end": 558, "text": "The Public Prosecutor ’ s Office has jurisdiction in all the Republic of Honduras , and all persons and legal entities have access"}, "D7S1": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d06", "start": 0, "end": 186, "text": "Supreme Electoral Tribunal (Guatemala) The Supreme Electoral Tribunal (officially: Supreme Electoral Tribunal of the Republic of Guatemala) is the highest authority in electoral matters."}, "D7S2": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d06", "start": 187, "end": 313, "text": "It is an independent constitutional body of political control, therefore, it is not subordinated to any organism of the State."}, "D7S3": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d06", "start": 314, "end": 424, "text": "This is governed by the Electoral and Political Parties Law, Decree 1-85 of the National Constituent Assembly."}, "D7S4": {"document_number": 7, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d06", "start": 425, "end": 655, "text": "This institution has the power to hold the elections for the office of President of the Republic and Vice President of the Republic, for the positions of Deputies to the Congress of the Republic and the Central American Parliament"}, "D8S1": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d07", "start": 0, "end": 155, "text": "la agricultura Standards Quizzes Press Releases My Account The Associated Press is an independent global news organization dedicated to factual reporting ."}, "D8S2": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d07", "start": 156, "end": 351, "text": "Founded in 1846 , AP today remains the most trusted source of fast , accurate , unbiased news in all formats and the essential provider of the technology and services vital to the news business ."}, "D8S3": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d07", "start": 352, "end": 422, "text": "More than half the world ’ s population sees AP journalism every day ."}, "D8S4": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d07", "start": 423, "end": 487, "text": "twitter instagram facebook Copyright 2025 The Associated Press ."}, "D8S5": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d07", "start": 488, "end": 509, "text": "All Rights Reserved ."}, "D8S6": {"document_number": 8, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d07", "start": 510, "end": 626, "text": "World News Guatemala prosecutor seeks to strip electoral authorities of immunity after election Guatemala prosecutor"}, "D9S1": {"document_number": 9, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d08", "start": 0, "end": 144, "text": "state receives all of the state 's electoral votes , there is a clear incentive to focus almost exclusively on only a few key undecided states ."}, "D9S2": {"document_number": 9, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d08", "start": 145, "end": 372, "text": "[ 251 ] Not all votes count the same [ edit ] Each state gets a minimum of three electoral votes , regardless of population , which has increasingly given low-population states more electors per voter ( or more voting power ) ."}, "D9S3": {"document_number": 9, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d08", "start": 373, "end": 494, "text": "[ 258 ] [ 259 ] For example , an electoral vote represents nearly four times as many people in California as in Wyoming ."}, "D9S4": {"document_number": 9, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d08", "start": 495, "end": 508, "text": "[ 258 ] [ 260"}, "D10S1": {"document_number": 10, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d09", "start": 0, "end": 93, "text": "in international trafficking are better resourced than the state authorities combating them ."}, "D10S2": {"document_number": 10, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d09", "start": 94, "end": 293, "text": "Although gang members have been arrested for selling drugs at the street level , it is still unclear how much interaction they have with the larger drug cartels and their operations within Honduras ."}, "D10S3": {"document_number": 10, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d09", "start": 294, "end": 313, "text": "[ 16 ] Some [ who ?"}, "D10S4": {"document_number": 10, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d09", "start": 314, "end": 451, "text": "] would use this argument to justify increasing US military aid to Honduras to help fight the organised drug gangs , while others [ who ?"}, "D10S5": {"document_number": 10, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d09", "start": 452, "end": 577, "text": "] claim that Honduras would be better off legalizing drugs , thus avoiding military solutions to Honduran security problems ."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "Brazil", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d00:c0", "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d01:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C1", "answer": "Canada", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C2", "answer": "Honduras", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d04:c0"]}, {"candidate_id": "C3", "answer": "Guatemala", "card_ids": ["ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d06:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d00", "card_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d00:c0", "entity": "Superior Electoral Court", "scope": "Country of jurisdiction", "claim": "The Superior Electoral Court (TSE) is the highest body of the Brazilian Electoral Justice.", "answer": "Brazil", "quote": "Superior Electoral Court The Superior Electoral Court (, TSE) is the highest body of the Brazilian Electoral Justice, which also comprises one Regional Electoral Court (, TRE) in each of the 26 states and the Federal District of the country, as determined by Article 118 of the Constitution of Brazil.", "original_document_number": 1}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d01", "card_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d01:c0", "entity": "Superior Electoral Court", "scope": "highest judicial body of the Brazilian Electoral Justice", "claim": "The Superior Electoral Court is the highest judicial body of the Brazilian Electoral Justice.", "answer": "Brazil", "quote": "The Superior Electoral Court is the highest judicial body of the Brazilian Electoral Justice as per the §3 of the Article 121 of the Brazilian", "original_document_number": 2}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03", "card_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d03:c0", "entity": "Supreme Electoral Tribunal", "scope": "Country", "claim": "The Supreme Electoral Tribunal belongs to Canada.", "answer": "Canada", "quote": "Canada Supreme Electoral Tribunal  \nThe Supreme Electoral Tribunal in Canada oversees the electoral process and ensures fair elections.", "original_document_number": 4}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d04", "card_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d04:c0", "entity": "Supreme Electoral Tribunal", "scope": "Country", "claim": "The Supreme Electoral Tribunal is the highest electoral authority in the Republic of Honduras.", "answer": "Honduras", "quote": "Supreme Electoral Tribunal (Honduras) The Supreme Electoral Tribunal (\"Tribunal Supremo Electoral\" in Spanish) is the highest electoral authority, both at the administrative and jurisdictional level in the Republic of Honduras. The Supreme Electoral Tribunal of Honduras deals with everything related to electoral acts and procedures.", "original_document_number": 5}, {"doc_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d06", "card_id": "ramdocs-0496-1f41320ff295:d06:c0", "entity": "Supreme Electoral Tribunal", "scope": "Country of affiliation", "claim": "The Supreme Electoral Tribunal (officially: Supreme Electoral Tribunal of the Republic of Guatemala) is the highe